# Rank 1526 / CVE-2023-41887: OpenRefine's database extension
# assembled its JDBC URLs by concatenation, so connection settings
# carrying URL metacharacters injected structure and connector
# parameters into the connection string (improper neutralization of
# special elements in a URL, CWE-74/CWE-150 family; fixed in 3.7.4).
# DatabaseCommand.getJdbcConfiguration fills a DatabaseConfiguration
# straight from the database-connection form
# (`jdbcConfig.setDatabaseName(request.getParameter("initialDatabase"))`
# and five siblings), and every connection manager then built
# `return "jdbc:" + dbConfig.getDatabaseType().toLowerCase() + "://" +
# dbConfig.getDatabaseHost() + ((port == 0) ? "" : (":" + port)) + "/"
# + dbConfig.getDatabaseName();` -- a name like
# "db?allowLoadLocalInfile=true" changes what the connector connects
# to. Pool commit 693fde606d is the real fix (COMMIT_OK -- "Properly
# escape JDBC URL components in database extension"):
# DatabaseConfiguration gains toURI(), which builds the URL through
# java.net.URI's five-argument constructor -- each component in its
# syntactic slot, percent-encoded by URI -- and every manager calls
# databaseConfiguration.toURI().toString() instead of concatenating.
# No pool correction.
#
# ## What fires, both revisions
#
# Three --cache off runs per revision over extensions/database (54
# java files) report **30 findings each, deterministically, with
# byte-identical by-rule sets on the vulnerable parent and the fixed
# 693fde606d**: 23 VYQL-INJ-009, 3 VYQL-INJ-001, 2 VYQL-INJ-134,
# 1 VYQL-PATH-055, 1 VYQL-CRY-003 -- all in module/scripts/index/*.js
# and in the servlet commands (HttpInput -> LogOutput), none on any
# connection manager. Scanned alone, all four connection managers
# report **zero findings at both revisions**. The full findings view
# was read, not the `-flags` only view. The 1st pass's zero was real.
#
# ## Why nothing ships
#
# The 1st pass called this a vocabulary gap ("no binding labels
# object-field reads as input"). It is an engine gap, and no binding
# can close it, because the store emits no node at all.
#
# * `jvConv.exprStmt` (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/java.go:296)
#   lowers `assignment_expression` to `nir.Assign` **only when the
#   left side is an identifier**; every other left side --
#   `this.name = x`, `dbConfig.name = x`, `c.name = x` -- falls
#   through to `nir.ExprStmt{Value: right}`, keeping the right-hand
#   side and discarding the store target entirely. `vyql graph` on
#   `this.name = request.getParameter("x"); exec("ls " + this.name)`
#   shows the read lowering to `Attr path=this.name` with an edge
#   into the sink argument, and the source `Call` with no outgoing
#   edge -- the write side produced nothing to carry it.
# * `nir.Assign.Targets` is `[]string` (internal/extract/nir/nir.go:179),
#   so the IR has no form for an attribute-targeted store. Carrying
#   taint from a field store to a later field load is a new dataflow
#   relation -- at minimum path-keyed, and in this rank's real shape
#   interprocedural through `setDatabaseName`/`getDatabaseName` on
#   `this` -- not a localized correction to a known construct.
#
# Probe A/B, binding edited into the tree and then reverted (the
# `-bindings` overlay is not a usable route): a sink binding
# `callee.method == "getConnection"` emitting `sink code.UrlFetch at
# args[0]` is enough to make the local-variable hop report
# VYQL-RF-001 HIGH. With that probe loaded the real
# extensions/database tree still reports the same 30 findings and
# **zero VYQL-RF-001 at both revisions** -- the taint dies inside
# DatabaseConfiguration's fields. The probe is also inert on
# artemis-unit-test-support (0 of 29+ findings) and opennms-tools
# (0 of 29), both of which concatenate `"jdbc:" +` values into
# DriverManager.getConnection: no UserControlledData reaches that
# argument on real code, so the sink binding alone would be an inert
# definition change, and a presence binding on the `"jdbc:" +
# concatenation shape has no provenance signal at all -- 154 files
# across the clone set carry that literal concatenation, essentially
# all of them ordinary hostnames, constants and test databases.
#
# Minimal pair, probe in place, same source and same sink labels in
# both: `String url = "jdbc:mysql://" + request.getParameter(..) +
# "/" + request.getParameter(..); DriverManager.getConnection(url, ..)`
# reports VYQL-RF-001 HIGH; the identical code with the value hops
# through `setDatabaseName(..)`/`getDatabaseName()` reports nothing.
# Only the field hop differs, so the construct is isolated. When
# attribute-targeted stores lower and a connection-string sink lands,
# the first and third blocks below must flip to expect.
#
# No definition change shipped. ENGINE-GAPS.md entry proposed: the
# field-store discard in jvConv.exprStmt, shared with the member-store
# pseudo-call the 1521 recheck traced in JavaScript, and with Python,
# whose apparent field-hop coverage is the DynamicSqlQuery /
# DynamicCommandExec pattern rules rather than taint.
#
# ## Recheck measurements (knowledge base tip d4e83b98f)
#
# Baseline 3x3 over extensions/database: 30/30/30 vulnerable,
# 30/30/30 fixed, identical by-rule sets. Connection managers scanned
# alone: 0 at both revisions, all four. Probe A/B: local hop 1
# VYQL-RF-001, field hop 0, real tree 0 VYQL-RF-001 at both
# revisions, artemis-unit-test-support 0, opennms-tools 0. Narrow
# spec passing with -v. Rank stays ATTENTION.

test "rank1526: form values hop the config object into the connection url"
  lang java
  file extensions/database/src/com/google/refine/extension/database/mysql/MySQLConnectionManager.java
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  package com.google.refine.extension.database.mysql;

  import java.sql.Connection;
  import java.sql.DriverManager;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;

  public class MySQLConnectionManager {

      public Connection getConnection(DatabaseConfiguration dbConfig) throws Exception {
          String dbURL = getDatabaseUrl(dbConfig);
          return DriverManager.getConnection(dbURL, dbConfig.getDatabaseUser(), dbConfig.getDatabasePassword());
      }

      private String getDatabaseUrl(DatabaseConfiguration dbConfig) {
          int port = dbConfig.getDatabasePort();
          return "jdbc:" + dbConfig.getDatabaseType().toLowerCase() + "://" + dbConfig.getDatabaseHost()
                  + ((port == 0) ? "" : (":" + port)) + "/" + dbConfig.getDatabaseName();
      }

      public DatabaseConfiguration getJdbcConfiguration(HttpServletRequest request) {
          DatabaseConfiguration jdbcConfig = new DatabaseConfiguration();
          jdbcConfig.setDatabaseHost(request.getParameter("databaseServer"));
          jdbcConfig.setDatabaseName(request.getParameter("initialDatabase"));
          return jdbcConfig;
      }
  }

  class DatabaseConfiguration {

      private String databaseHost;
      private String databaseName;

      void setDatabaseHost(String host) {
          this.databaseHost = host;
      }

      void setDatabaseName(String name) {
          this.databaseName = name;
      }

      String getDatabaseHost() {
          return this.databaseHost;
      }

      String getDatabaseName() {
          return this.databaseName;
      }

      String getDatabaseType() {
          return "mysql";
      }

      int getDatabasePort() {
          return 0;
      }

      String getDatabaseUser() {
          return "refine";
      }

      String getDatabasePassword() {
          return "refine";
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1526: the fixed revision builds the url through uri components"
  lang java
  file extensions/database/src/com/google/refine/extension/database/mysql/MySQLConnectionManager.java
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  package com.google.refine.extension.database.mysql;

  import java.net.URI;
  import java.net.URISyntaxException;
  import java.sql.Connection;
  import java.sql.DriverManager;

  public class MySQLConnectionManager {

      public Connection getConnection(DatabaseConfiguration dbConfig) throws Exception {
          String dbURL = dbConfig.toURI().toString();
          return DriverManager.getConnection(dbURL, dbConfig.getDatabaseUser(), dbConfig.getDatabasePassword());
      }
  }

  class DatabaseConfiguration {
      public URI toURI() {
          try {
              return new URI(
                      "jdbc:" + databaseType.toLowerCase(),
                      databaseHost + ((databasePort == 0) ? "" : (":" + databasePort)),
                      "/" + databaseName,
                      useSSL ? "useSSL=true" : null,
                      null
              );
          } catch (URISyntaxException e) {
              throw new IllegalArgumentException(e);
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1526: a field store carries the parameter into the url argument"
  lang java
  file extensions/database/src/com/google/refine/extension/database/mysql/MySQLConnectionManager.java
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  package com.google.refine.extension.database.mysql;

  import java.sql.Connection;
  import java.sql.DriverManager;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;

  public class FieldHopConnectionManager {

      private String databaseName;

      public Connection connect(HttpServletRequest request) throws Exception {
          setDatabaseName(request.getParameter("initialDatabase"));
          String dbURL = "jdbc:mysql://localhost/" + getDatabaseName();
          return DriverManager.getConnection(dbURL, "refine", "refine");
      }

      void setDatabaseName(String name) {
          this.databaseName = name;
      }

      String getDatabaseName() {
          return this.databaseName;
      }
  }
  ```
